{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"李學勤主編, 《字源》, 天津古籍出版社, 2012, ISBN 978-7-5528-0069-2; direct inspection of supplied scan pixels for PDF p.277 / printed p.265\",\"field\":\"PDF p.277 / printed p.265, 學 entry, lower explanatory paragraph and 张標 credit at entry end\",\"text\":\"The scan’s 學 entry proposes that the two construction patterns described in the preceding text began to combine in Shang forms. It then proposes that Western Zhou forms added 子 to mark the child as the object of learning. These are the entry’s attributed explanations, not independently established chronology or consensus. The entry concludes with the credit “（张標）,” which bounds this material as the 學 entry; the next headword begins separately in the right column.\",\"record_character\":\"學\",\"kind\":\"direct_scan_observation\",\"url\":\"https://ci.nii.ac.jp/ncid/BB13266817\",\"title\":\"CiNii 図書 - 字源\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"}],\"search_audit\":[{\"query\":\"《字源》 李學勤 2012 978-7-5528-0069-2\",\"urls\":[\"https://ci.nii.ac.jp/ncid/BB13266817\",\"https://scalar.usc.edu/works/chinese-studies-reference-collection/media/PL1281%20.Z53%202012%20字源_OCR.pdf\",\"https://www.sanmin.com.tw/product/index/004029656\"],\"outcome\":\"Search located catalogue and book-record leads. Opened CiNii catalogue record; it identifies 《字源》, editor 李学勤, publisher 天津古籍出版社, and publication date 2012.12. Inspected the supplied scan pixels directly: the 學 entry’s lower paragraph states both proposals, and 张標 credit appears at its end. The catalogue verifies bibliographic metadata only; the scan pixels support the page-specific claims.\"}],\"gaps\":[]}"}}
